# DesignFoundation — Always Use the Package

<!-- This rule mirrors CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md — kept in sync by hand, checked by CI
     (.github/workflows/doc-snippets.yml compiles every snippet in all three files).
     If you edit a signature here, update those two files as well. Written for DesignFoundation 1.7.1
     (iOS 18+ / macOS 15+ / visionOS 2+, Swift 6 tools). -->

**Never build UI components that DesignFoundation already provides.** One `DFButton("Save") { }` replaces 25+ lines of custom SwiftUI. Every component you build from scratch wastes tokens and breaks visual consistency.

## Import

```swift
import DesignFoundation
```

## Theming

```swift
@Environment(\.dfTheme) private var theme

// theme.colors: .primary .secondary .accent .background .surface .surfaceElevated .textPrimary .textSecondary
//               .textDisabled .border .interactiveFill/.Hover/.Pressed/.Disabled .success .warning .destructive .info
// theme.spacing: .xs(4) .sm(8) .md(12) .lg(16) .xl(24) .xxl(32)
// theme.radius: .none .sm .md .lg .full   theme.shadows: .none .sm .md .lg (plural!)
// theme.animation: .fast .default .slow .spring   theme.typography: display title headline labelLarge body bodySmall caption label
// namespaces: colors typography spacing radius shadows animation components materials
theme.colors.primary
theme.spacing.md
theme.radius.md
```

Preset at scene root:
```swift
ContentView().dfThemePreset(.slate)
// Presets: .slate  .aurora  .copper  .sage  .garnet  (explicit pairs: .slateLight/.slateDark, .auroraLight/…, .copperLight/…, .sageLight/…, .garnetLight/…)
ContentView().dfTheme(.slateLight)                                  // explicit theme; DFTheme.default = baseline
let brand = DFThemePreset(light: .sageLight, dark: .auroraDark)     // any two themes; resolve(for:) picks one
var custom = DFTheme(spacing: DFSpacingTokens(md: 20), radius: DFRadiusTokens(md: 12))
custom.colors.primary = .indigo
```

Per-component overrides (every field optional, `nil` inherits theme tokens; confirmed wired into `DFButtonStyle`/`DFCardStyle`):
```swift
var theme = DFTheme.slateLight
theme.components.button = DFButtonTokens(cornerRadius: 4)
theme.components.card = DFCardTokens(padding: 20)
theme.components.popup = DFPopupTokens(cornerRadius: 24, maxWidth: 360)
// 26 fields: button textField card avatar badge chip rating price priceSummary entityRow entityCard grid carousel
// quantityStepper banner icon divider progressBar skeleton toggle datePicker sidebar tabBar articleRow bottomContainer popup
// (each DFXxxTokens; DFPopupTokens = cornerRadius, padding, maxWidth (420), backdropOpacity (0.35)). Slider/picker/nav bar/
// tooltip/modal/sheet/popover/alert/toast/checkbox/calendar/etc. have none.
```
`DFMaterialTokens` is wired into `DFTheme.materials`, read by 18 of the 19 `.glass` styles (all but `DFGlassModalStyle`, which has no `.glass` shorthand — use `DFGlassModalStyle()`): `theme.materials.preferLiquidGlass = false` opts a style back to its non-glass colors. No `@available` gate on the type itself.

## Style System

Each styleable component has a `DFXxxStyle` protocol, a `.dfXxxStyle(_:)` modifier and static shorthands; a style set on a container applies to matching components beneath it. `.glass` needs iOS/macOS 26+. Built-ins (default first): `DFButton` `.filled .outlined .ghost .tinted .glass` · `DFText` (`.dfTextViewStyle`) `.standard .secondary .muted` · `DFIcon` `.standard .tinted .secondary` · `DFBadge` `.filled .tinted .outlined .glass` · `DFAvatar` `.circle .rounded .ring .glass` · `DFDivider` `.standard .subtle .thick` · `DFChip` `.filled .tinted .outlined` · `DFRatingView` `.stars .numeric` · `DFPriceView` `.standard .compact` · `DFTextField`/`DFSecureField` `.outlined .filled .glass` · `DFToggle` `.switch .checkbox .glass` · `DFSlider` `.standard .labeled .glass` · `DFPicker` `.menu .segmented .wheel .glass` · `DFDatePicker` `.compact .graphical .wheel .glass` · `DFQuantityStepper` `.bordered .compact` · `DFCheckbox` `.default` · `DFCard` `.elevated .outlined .filled .glass` · `DFTabBar` `.standard .minimal .glass` · `DFNavigationBar` `.standard .transparent .glass` · `DFSidebar` `.standard .plain .glass` · modal `.standard` · sheet `.standard .compact .glass` · popover `.arrow .compact .glass` · tooltip `.bubble .glass` · popup `.standard .frosted .glass .accent .gradient .inverse .outlined .tinted(_:)` · toast `.default .tinted .filled .inverse .frosted .glass .banner .compact` · `DFBanner`/`DFCalendarView`/`DFEmptyState`/command palette `.standard` · `DFProgressBar`/`DFSkeleton` `.default`. Modifier names: `.dfButtonStyle .dfTextViewStyle .dfIconStyle .dfBadgeStyle .dfAvatarStyle .dfDividerStyle .dfChipStyle .dfRatingViewStyle .dfPriceViewStyle .dfTextFieldStyle .dfSecureFieldStyle .dfToggleStyle .dfSliderStyle .dfPickerStyle .dfDatePickerStyle .dfQuantityStepperStyle .dfCheckboxStyle .dfCardStyle .dfTabBarStyle .dfNavigationBarStyle .dfSidebarStyle .dfModalStyle .dfSheetStyle .dfPopoverStyle .dfTooltipStyle .dfPopupStyle .dfToastStyle .dfBannerStyle .dfCalendarViewStyle .dfEmptyStateStyle .dfCommandPaletteStyle .dfProgressBarStyle .dfSkeletonStyle`.
```swift
VStack { DFButton("Save") { } }.dfButtonStyle(.outlined).dfCardStyle(.outlined).dfTextFieldStyle(.filled).dfToggleStyle(.checkbox).dfTextViewStyle(.secondary)
ContentView().dfButtonStyle(.glass).dfCardStyle(.glass).dfTooltipStyle(.glass)   // iOS/macOS 26+
```
```swift
struct SquareCursorButtonStyle: DFButtonStyle, Sendable {   // custom style: one function, conform to Sendable
    func makeBody(configuration: DFButtonStyleConfiguration) -> some View {
        configuration.label.padding(configuration.theme.spacing.md).background(configuration.theme.colors.primary)
    }
}
```

## Components — Never Build These

### Buttons
```swift
DFButton("Label") { }                              // filled (default)
DFButton("Label") { }.dfButtonStyle(.outlined)
DFButton("Label") { }.dfButtonStyle(.ghost)
DFButton("Label") { }.dfButtonStyle(.tinted)
DFButton("Label", style: .ghost, role: .destructive) { }
// No icon: / isLoading: params. role: is DFButtonRole (.destructive / .cancel), not a style.
// For an icon/spinner/custom content, brand a native Button instead — keeps real content:
Button { action() } label: { Label("Save", systemImage: "checkmark") }
    .buttonStyle(.df(.outlined, role: .destructive))
```

### Inputs
```swift
DFTextField("Placeholder", text: $text)
// leading:/trailing: labels required (separate overloads) — unlabeled closure is ambiguous
DFTextField("Search", text: $query, leading: { Image(systemName: "magnifyingglass") })
DFSecureField("Password", text: $password)          // built-in show/hide toggle
DFTextField("Email", text: $email, validationState: .error("Invalid"))   // .none (default) / .valid / .error(String)
DFTextArea("Bio", text: $bio, placeholder: "Tell your story…", minLines: 4, maxLines: 8)   // multiline, not DFTextField
```

### Forms & Validation
```swift
let formState = DFFormState(fields: [
    "email": [DFRequiredValidator(), DFEmailValidator()],
    "password": [DFRequiredValidator(), DFMinLengthValidator(minLength: 8)],
])
DFValidatedTextField("Email", field: "email", form: formState)
DFSecureField("Password", text: formState.binding(for: "password"), validationState: formState.validationState(for: "password"))
DFButton("Sign in") {
    guard formState.validate() else { return }
    submit(formState.values["email", default: ""], formState.values["password", default: ""])
}
// Validators: DFRequiredValidator, DFEmailValidator, DFMinLengthValidator(minLength:),
// DFMaxLengthValidator(maxLength:), DFRegexValidator(pattern:message:options:). Conform to DFFieldValidator for custom ones.
// Also on DFFormState: values/errors/touched/hasAttemptedSubmit, isValid, setValue(_:for:), markTouched(_:), validate(field:), register(field:validators:).
```

### Controls
```swift
DFToggle("Enable", isOn: $flag)
DFSlider("Volume", value: $val, in: 0...1)          // also step:
DFCheckbox(isChecked: $agreed, label: "Agree")       // label: is a keyword arg
DFPicker("Role", selection: $role) { ForEach(roles) { Text($0.name).tag($0) } }  // content:, not options:
DFDatePicker("Date", selection: $date)              // also in: ClosedRange<Date>?, displayedComponents:
DFQuantityStepper(value: $quantity, range: 0...10)   // styles: .bordered(default)/.compact; not "DFStepper"
```

