### Feedback & Overlays
```swift
YourContentView().dfAlert(isPresented: $show, configuration: DFAlertConfiguration(title: "Title", message: "…", actions: [
    DFAlertAction(title: "Cancel", role: .cancel),
]))
YourContentView().dfAlert(isPresented: $show, title: "Saved", message: "Done.")   // shorthand; actions default to one "OK"
DFToastQueue.shared.show(text: "Saved", severity: .success)   // text:, severity: — not style:; duration 3 s; queues one at a time
ContentView().dfToast(queue: DFToastQueue.shared)
// DFPopupConfiguration(kind:position:transition:animation:autoDismissAfter:dismissOnTap:dismissOnOutsideTap:dismissOnDrag:dimsBackground:backdrop:)
// kind .center(default) .toast .floater .sheet(always bottom); transition .automatic .slide .scale .fade .none .asymmetric(insert:remove:);
// presets .centered .toast(position:autoDismissAfter:) .floater(position:) .sheet(backdrop:); dismissOnOutsideTap/dimsBackground default true.
YourContentView()
    .dfPopup(isPresented: $show) { Text("Centered card") }
    .dfPopup(isPresented: $show, configuration: .toast(position: .bottom)) { Text("Edge toast") }
    .dfPopup(isPresented: $show, configuration: .floater(position: .bottomTrailing)) { Text("Floater") }
    .dfPopup(item: $selectedItem) { item in Text(item.title) }   // Identifiable item
DFToastQueue.shared.show(text: "Saved", severity: .success, position: .bottom)   // position: 9 values, default .top
// ORDER MATTERS: popup/toast layers are overlays owned by .dfPopup/.dfToast and read the environment from outside them —
// apply .dfPopupStyle/.dfToastStyle and .dfTheme/.dfThemePreset AFTER (outside) .dfPopup/.dfToast, not before.
YourContentView().dfPopup(isPresented: $show) { Text("Themed") }.dfPopupStyle(.frosted).dfThemePreset(.slate)
YourContentView().dfPopupStyle(.frosted)   // per-popup tokens: theme.components.popup (DFPopupTokens). .standard .frosted .glass(26+) .accent .gradient .inverse .outlined .tinted(.success)
YourContentView().dfPopup(isPresented: $showPopup, configuration: .sheet(backdrop: .blur)) { Text("Sheet") }   // DFPopupBackdrop .none/.dim/.blur wins over dimsBackground
YourContentView().dfPopup(isPresented: $showPopup) {
    DFPopupCard(icon: "sparkles", title: "Upgrade", message: "Unlock Pro.", primaryAction: DFPopupAction("Upgrade") { }, secondaryAction: DFPopupAction("Later") { }, onClose: { showPopup = false })
}   // hero: DFPopupCard(title:media:content:) — media bleeds to the edges
YourContentView().dfToast(style: .tinted)   // (not .dfToastStyle(_:).dfToast()) // .default .tinted .filled .inverse .frosted .glass(26+) .banner .compact
DFToastQueue.shared.show(text: "Moved to the trash", severity: .error, title: "Deleted", actionTitle: "Undo", action: { restore() })   // action runs, then the toast dismisses
YourContentView().dfToast().dfToastStyle(.compact)   // also fine: style applied outside the toast layer
ZStack { YourContentView() }.overlay { DFPopupHost(isPresented: $showPopup, configuration: .centered) { Text("Hosted") } }   // embed the popup layer in a custom container
DFBanner(icon: "info.circle.fill", message: "New version available.", severity: .info, isDismissible: true, onDismiss: { })   // NOT DFToastQueue-based, place directly in hierarchy

// Overlays are modifiers, not constructible views — no DFModal(isPresented:) etc.
YourContentView()
    .dfModal(isPresented: $show) { content }
    .dfFullscreenModal(isPresented: $show) { content }   // full-screen cover variant
    .dfSheet(isPresented: $show) { content }
    .dfPopover(isPresented: $show, attachmentAnchor: .point(.bottom), arrowEdge: .top) { content }
    .dfTooltip("Hint", delay: 0.5, placement: .bottom)   // plain String, no separate trigger view; placement .top(default) .bottom .leading .trailing

YourContentView().dfCommandPalette(isPresented: $showPalette, items: [
    DFCommandPaletteItem(title: "New Document", icon: "doc.badge.plus"),
], placeholder: "Search…") { selected in handle(selected) }
// Case-insensitive substring filter (also public: DFCommandPaletteFilter.filter(items:query:)); ↑/↓/Return/Escape nav on macOS. Only .standard style.
```

## Supporting Types
`DFButtonRole`/`DFAlertActionRole` (.destructive .cancel) · `DFValidationState` (.none .valid .error(String)) · `DFTextScale` (.display .title .headline .labelLarge .body .bodySmall .label .caption; via `DFTextStyle`) · `DFBadgeVariant` (.numeric(Int) .dot .text(String)) · `DFAvatarSource` · `DFAvatarPresence` (.none .online .away .busy) · `DFIconSource` · `DFChipVariant` (.label .labelWithIcon .dismissible .selectable) · `DFRatingMode` (.readOnly .interactive(onChange:)) · `DFDividerOrientation` · `DFProgressBarVariant` · `DFSkeletonShape` · `DFGridColumns` · `DFPriceLineItemEmphasis` · `DFEntityMedia` · `DFEntityTrailing` · `DFNavigationBarDisplayMode` · `DFTooltipPlacement` · `DFDataTableSelectionMode` · `DFDataGridLargeDatasetStrategy` · `DFPopupKind` · `DFPopupPosition` · `DFPopupTransition` · `DFPopupBackdrop` · `DFPopupCardAlignment` (.center .leading) · `DFPopupIconTint` (.brand .soft .severity(_:)) · `DFPopupIconBadge`/`DFPopupHeader`/`DFPopupActions` (pieces of `DFPopupCard`) · `DFToastSeverity` · `DFToastMessage` · `DFToastLayout` (.floating .flush) · `DFShadow`/`DFShadowTokens`/`DFColorTokens`/`DFTypographyTokens`/`DFSpacingTokens`/`DFRadiusTokens`/`DFAnimationTokens`/`DFMaterialTokens`/`DFComponentTokens`. Style protocols (each has `AnyDFXxxStyle` + `DFXxxStyleConfiguration`): DFButtonStyle DFTextViewStyle DFIconStyle DFBadgeStyle DFAvatarStyle DFDividerStyle DFChipStyle DFRatingViewStyle DFPriceViewStyle DFTextFieldStyle DFSecureFieldStyle DFToggleStyle DFSliderStyle DFPickerStyle DFDatePickerStyle DFQuantityStepperStyle DFCheckboxStyle DFCardStyle DFTabBarStyle DFNavigationBarStyle DFSidebarStyle DFModalStyle DFSheetStyle DFPopoverStyle DFTooltipStyle DFPopupStyle DFToastStyle DFBannerStyle DFCalendarViewStyle DFEmptyStateStyle DFCommandPaletteStyle DFProgressBarStyle DFSkeletonStyle; `.buttonStyle(.df(_:role:))` returns `DFBrandedButtonStyle`. Token structs at `theme.components`: DFButtonTokens DFTextFieldTokens DFCardTokens DFAvatarTokens DFBadgeTokens DFChipTokens DFRatingTokens DFPriceTokens DFPriceSummaryTokens DFEntityRowTokens DFEntityCardTokens DFGridTokens DFCarouselTokens DFQuantityStepperTokens DFBannerTokens DFIconTokens DFDividerTokens DFProgressBarTokens DFSkeletonTokens DFToggleTokens DFDatePickerTokens DFSidebarTokens DFTabBarTokens DFArticleRowTokens DFBottomContainerTokens DFPopupTokens. `DFDataTableColumn` = typealias of `DFTableColumn`.

## Cross-Platform

**You do not need `#if os()` to use any DF component.** Platform differences are handled internally via `DFPlatformContext` (`@Environment(\.dfPlatformContext)`: `idiom`, `horizontalSizeClass`, `isLiquidGlassAvailable`) — `DFSidebar`, `DFTabBar` and every overlay modifier adapt automatically. `DFPlatformVariant` is declared but not consumed by any built-in component in 1.7.1; don't rely on it.

The only place you need guards is in your own app-level code calling APIs DF doesn't wrap:

```swift
// Your own scene declarations only
#if os(macOS)
WindowGroup("Detail", id: "detail", for: String.self) { $id in DetailView(id: id ?? "") }
    .defaultSize(width: 900, height: 700).windowStyle(.titleBar)
#endif

// URL — always use cross-platform environment action
@Environment(\.openURL) private var openURL
openURL(url)    // never NSWorkspace.shared.open()
```

